  "command": "xxd",
  "help": "Usage: xxd [OPTION]... [INFILE [OUTFILE]]\nDisplay bytes or reverse an addressed, plain, or binary dump.\n{{help:autoskip:0}}\n{{help:bits:0}}\n{{help:little:0}}\n{{help:ebcdic:0}}\n{{help:group:0}}\n{{help:upper:0}}\n{{help:offset:0}}\n{{help:plain:0}}\n{{help:include:0}}\n{{help:reverse:0}}\n{{help:cols:0}}\n{{help:len:0}}\n{{help:seek:0}}\n{{help:name:0}}\n{{help:help:0}}\n{{help:version:0}}\n\nProject aliases: --little/-littleendian select -e; --ebcdic/-ebcdic select -E.\nProject long-option syntax also accepts =VALUE for --cols, --group, --len,\n{{help:name:1}}\n-h/--help use the project metadata contract: stdout and status 0.\n\nUsage errors exit 1; runtime errors retain their command-specific statuses.\nOption values and operands after -- remain literal.\n",
